{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"fields":{"description":"## Context / Problem\nTwelve integration-test files contain 51 audited blocks with repeated, historical, ornamental, or duplicated prose. Scope and line anchors are revalidated on `origin/main` at `0033662b5534531d84e39d4a14bf75c8e768e85e`.\n\n## Approach\nCondense only the listed blocks. Preserve non-docstring AST, all runtime strings/assertions/subprocess programs, test directives, and exact concurrency or recovery semantics.\n\n## Scope\n- `s3_doctor_harness.py:1-21` — Preserve real local Git bundles, injected S3 surface, locking/exclusions, and lossless reachability.\n- `test_b636_rebuild_history_loss.py:1-12,279-282` — Preserve snapshot-only state, missing/retired-source fail-closed recovery, and per-UUID fallback.\n- `test_bare_repository_fixture_portability_heldout.py:1-71,94-98` — Preserve `safe.bareRepository=explicit`, accepted top-level `--git-dir`, AST/dataflow scanner, positional propagation, and exemptions; remove repeated self-exclusion history.\n- `test_concurrency_regression.py:1-19,79-90,102-112,121-142,148-164,324-330,422-426,442-456,549-551,587-591,804-813,1054-1061,1325-1328,1374-1380,1420-1425,1492-1501,1506-1517,1619-1634,1665-1676,1721-1724,1755-1767,1851-1855,1876-1880,1904-1924,2190-2198` — Preserve independent stores/barriers, checked-precondition versus production reads, exact union/fork/HLC winners, post-lock recovery, retired-source repair, real CAS/push/fetch/merge evidence, parent-cascade ownership, and append-only sidecar convergence; delete conversational/repeated setup.\n- `test_ensure_project_mapping.py:1-17` and `test_id_collision.py:1-19` — Preserve seed/stamp/no-ticket-events state and canonical-ID/deterministic-alias collision coverage.\n- `test_prepare_reclaim_backup.py:639-656` — Preserve refusal of detached upkeep and probe-only trace.\n- `test_reconcile_live_e2e.py:1-42,59-67,78-80,84-92,328-334,394-412,462-476,523-529,571-577,595-606` — Preserve bilateral cleanup, xdist confinement, isolated imports, cache invalidation, key/summary fallback, bounded injected backoff, and real-client memoization; remove future-ticket narration.\n- `test_s3_doctor_heldout.py:1-21`, `test_s3_doctor.py:1-15,62,131-139,203-209`, and `test_s3_preflight.py:1-14` — Preserve held-out safety/conflict/locking inventory, lossless healing, bounded transient retry, published-ref exclusion, fail-closed S3/S3ZIP requirement, and helper-version seam; remove historical CI IDs.\n- `test_store_concurrency.py:1-19,131-135` — Preserve permanent dual-leg locking, all-writer event survival, and clean-fsck oracle.\n\nConsumers are pytest, integration/held-out suites, reusable harness imports, live-Jira confinement guards, and `check_comment_hygiene.py`; no target-specific runtime docstring reader exists. Preserve every listed `noqa`, `type: ignore`, and coverage directive byte-for-byte and attached to its statement.\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] Only reviewed comments/true docstrings or blank lines change; normalized non-docstring AST, runtime strings, assertions, and exact statement-attached directives remain unchanged.\n- [ ] An independent reviewer posts a leaf-linked TSV with one row per edited block, pinned before and immutable final-commit after citations, preserved contract/consumer, before/after words, and `semantic-preservation` plus `bloat-removal` verdicts.\n- [ ] Every edited block is shorter and removes repetition/history/ornament rather than relocating it; every TSV row is PASS.\n- [ ] Recorded focused hermetic checks, path-scoped `git diff --check`, and worktree-venv `make verify` pass.\n- [ ] Missing/FAIL rows or unmatched diff hunks block closure.\n\n## Verification\nRun the recorded normalized AST/directive guard, focused tests, diff check, and `make verify`. The independent TSV judges prose quality."}},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"EDIT","timestamp":1788613368502508001,"uuid":"f6c8d2c3-6644-45ed-9524-7d7b081befda"}